{
  "beat13": "Seren had named the finding of the one I had lost as the thing the rite must deliver, yet the softness she gave those words was shaped for the witnesses who watched her offer them. The current that answered pulled toward that same finding, but the shape it took carried the dread that it would arrive twisted by her need to be seen as the one who had given enough. I felt the direction of it settle under my ribs, the wrongness already naming itself in how the assembly leaned closer.",
  "beat20": "The staff was heavier than memory had prepared me for, the twin hooks balanced so perfectly that any shift in my grip changed the angle of both ends at once. I felt the eyes of the assembly on the object in my hands and on the place where the rite had turned. The question of what would happen next sat open in the air between us, and I could not yet see which direction the next voice would come from.",
  "postInterruptionBeat": "The Answer rested in my hands, its twin hooks balanced and waiting. The Dohkar’s ruling and Julian’s claim both hung in the air at once, and the assembly’s attention had returned to the staff I now held. I could feel every possible direction the next moment might take, each one carrying its own cost, and none of them yet spoken aloud."
}
